      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warrenton%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town takes its name from Warren County, which was named after Revolutionary War hero Joseph G.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.warrenton-mo.org/about/history/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "dropped_surname_no_wiki_source"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The first North Missouri Railroad train rolled into Warrenton on July 4, 1857, marking the town’s early connection to the rail network.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.warrenton-mo.org/about/history/",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Ernst Schowengerdt House and the Warren County Courthouse sit on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warrenton%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Every June, the Downtown Association hosts FrühlingFest, a celebration of the area’s German heritage with food, vendors, and family activities.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
